426: +# ---- #529 REPAIR 16: HARD_RESET's residue with the latch CLEAR (repair 15's pass 2) ----
427: +#  An accepted `sw'/`sd +0x08 = 0x0800' stops every CPU, and because the branch clears HARD_RESET before the residue
428: +#  test it prints nothing.  No row counted the CONTROL text in a session holding an accepted 0x0800 write, so a build
429: +#  that skipped that clear passed every row while the CPUs still stopped (table15a_20260926/).  The halt ends the
430: +#  guest's work, so the twin comes FIRST: 0x0001 (residue 0x1, one text), then 0x0800 as the session's last store.
431: +#  CHANNELS: the text count -- ONE on the fixed build, TWO if the clear is skipped -- and the halt: v1 left at the
432: +#  sentinel by the RAM trip that cannot run, which shows the 0x0800 write reached the arm.
